# Root build context (used by the `web` service, whose context is the repository root).
#
# Without this file, `COPY . .` copies the host's apps/web/node_modules over the
# node_modules the image just installed. Where a host package is a directory and
# the image's is a file (or vice versa) the daemon aborts with:
#   cannot copy to non-directory: .../apps/web/node_modules/@playwright/test
#
# NOTE: Docker reads the .dockerignore at the *context root* only. The api, worker
# and beat services build from ./backend, so they are governed by
# backend/.dockerignore, not this file.

# --- dependency trees (reinstalled inside the image) ------------------------
**/node_modules
**/.pnpm-store
**/.yarn/cache
**/.yarn/install-state.gz
**/bower_components

# --- JavaScript build output -----------------------------------------------
**/.next
**/out
**/dist
**/build
**/.turbo
**/.swc
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/storybook-static
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/.playwright

# --- Python virtual environments and caches --------------------------------
**/.venv
**/venv
**/env
**/ENV
**/virtualenv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*$py.class
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.tox
**/.nox
**/*.egg-info
**/.eggs

# --- coverage and profiling ------------------------------------------------
**/.coverage
**/.coverage.*
**/coverage
**/coverage.xml
**/htmlcov
**/.benchmarks
**/prof

# --- local secrets and environment ------------------------------------------
# .env.example is deliberately NOT excluded: it is documentation and carries no
# real values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.dev-keys
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
!**/testdata/*.pem
!**/testdata/*.key

# --- version control, CI and editor state ----------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
**/.git-orphaned
.vscode
.idea
**/*.swp
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db

# --- infrastructure state (never belongs in an image) ----------------------
**/.terraform
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
**/.terraform.lock.hcl

# --- local data and logs ----------------------------------------------------
**/*.log
**/*.rdb
**/pgdata
**/postgres-data
docs
*.md
!README.md

# --- superseded lockfile ----------------------------------------------------
# The project is pnpm (see `packageManager` in package.json). An npm lockfile left
# in the context would be dead weight and an invitation to build with the wrong
# tool; the Dockerfile now runs `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`.
apps/web/package-lock.json

# What is deliberately kept: all application source, package.json,
# pnpm-lock.yaml, pnpm-workspace.yaml, turbo.json, tsconfig, .eslintrc.*,
# vitest.config.ts, next.config.*, tailwind.config.*, postcss.config.* and
# next-env.d.ts.
